  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Learning Love**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Pandy**: back after 75 archived shows (843 days); rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **Bare Hands**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **Don't Get To Close**: back after 112 archived shows (1574 days); rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2008-01-24.hometeam.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 30 songs; 148 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **ween2008-01-24.mk41.flac24**: source not stated; 30 songs; 149 min [2]\n- **ween2008-01-24.4022.flac16**: source not stated; 30 songs; 150 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer attended; the venue was packed and the crowd was enthusiastic [4]\n- Microphones were clamped to a stand at the balcony rail, suspended three feet down on a gooseneck [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2008-01-24.hometeam.flac16**: taped by J.T. Lucchesi; transferred by J.T. Lucchesi; source: Peluso P Stereo (cardioids/xy, balcony front, 7-8'high, dfc) > Sound Devices 702 @ 24/44 [1]\n- **ween2008-01-24.mk41.flac24**: taped by Todd (titotito at gmail); transferred by Todd (titotito at gmail); source: mk41 > kc5 > cmc6 > m248 > mini-me > hd-p2 (24/96) [2]. Also: Recorded from the second-floor balcony with a DFC microphone pointed at the stacks, using a 7-foot clamp; 24-bit FLAC [2]\n- **ween2008-01-24.4022.flac16**: taped by Craig Davis; transferred by Craig Davis; source: B&K4022 (ortf) > Sonosax > 744T [3]. Also: Recorded with B&K 4022 mics in ORTF, through a Sonosax preamp to a 744T recorder; Transfer went from the 744T through Soundforge 7.0 for fades, resampling and dithering, then CD wave to FLAC; taped and transferred by Craig Davis [3]",
